<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<!--
  Typed-result sub-interface for a ReadIdentity Operation1. Exported on the
  same object path as the parent Operation1. The Result signal fires once,
  before Operation1.Finished, and only when the operation completed
  successfully (status == Ok).

  Payload shape: a{s a{s(sssv)}}
    outer key  group key       (e.g. "personal", "address", "document")
    inner key  field key       (e.g. "given_name", "date_of_birth")
    tuple      label_key       (localised-text key for the field label)
               label_fallback  (English fallback text)
               type            "text" | "date" | "binary"
               value           "s" for text/date, "ay" for binary
    Photo fields are OMITTED from this payload — clients call GetPhoto for
    the bytes, which arrive on the Photo1.Result signal as sealed memfds.

  Late-subscriber recovery — GetResult():
    The Result signal is a one-shot: a client that learns the op path only
    from the ReadIdentity() return may subscribe too late (a hot card session
    finishes the read faster than the client's match rules install) and would
    lose the payload forever. GetResult() re-serves the retained field map —
    the exact Result payload — while the operation is still within the
    cleanup-grace window AND finished Ok. Returns
    org.librescrs.Agent.Error.NoResult once the grace window has elapsed or
    when the operation did not finish Ok. Same recovery contract as
    Sign1.GetResult (the generic Operation1 terminal triple recovers only
    status/errorCode, never a payload). The retained identity fields live
    only in agent RAM until the operation is evicted (cleanup-grace GC, card
    removal, owner disconnect) — never persisted; same retention policy as
    the Sign1 artifact.

  Progressive delivery — Group(groupKey, fields):
    Fires zero or more times, in read order, strictly BEFORE Result above —
    one signal per field group as the card plugin produces it, ahead of the
    complete grouped Result this interface has always sent. `fields` is the
    SAME (sssv) tuple shape as one entry of Result's own outer map — one
    group's worth, not the whole grouped dict. This is a progressive HINT
    only: Result stays the complete, authoritative set regardless of what
    (if anything) streamed here, and a client that never subscribes to this
    signal at all loses nothing — it simply renders once Result arrives, the
    same as before this signal existed. There is no recovery pull for a
    missed Group signal (unlike GetResult above): a late subscriber that
    missed some or all of them still converges on the correct, complete
    result via Result/GetResult. Emitted only when the agent serves the
    "identity-stream" feature token (see Manager1.Features) — an agent
    predating it never sends this signal, so an older client build (which
    does not know this signal name at all) is simply never addressed by it.
-->
<node>
  <interface name="org.librescrs.Agent.Operation.Identity1">
    <signal name="Result">
      <arg name="fields" type="a{sa{s(sssv)}}"/>
    </signal>

    <signal name="Group">
      <arg name="groupKey" type="s"/>
      <arg name="fields" type="a{s(sssv)}"/>
    </signal>

    <method name="GetResult">
      <arg name="fields" type="a{sa{s(sssv)}}" direction="out"/>
    </method>
  </interface>
</node>
